PARITY (web source reproduced)
------------------------------------------------------------
- Data sources: useTranslation + useFormatting. The web component is a presentational
  leaf taking `metrics: DigestMetrics` from the parent useWeeklyDigest aggregation; the
  native surface binds the coalesced parent query snapshot through the P1/S8 state-holder
  seam (WeekOverWeekSource -> WeekOverWeekModel @Observable). No HTTP in the view.
- Composition: a GlassPanel titled "Week-over-Week Comparison" wrapping a responsive grid
  (web grid-cols-1 / sm:2 / lg:3 -> LazyVGrid adaptive) of SIX StatCards — Distance (km),
  Drives, Energy (kWh), Cost (currency), Efficiency (Wh/km), CO2 Saved (kg). Each card =
  label + SF-Symbol icon, value + unit, and the week-over-week trend (up/down/flat arrow +
  signed %). trendFor invert semantics reproduced exactly (energy/cost/efficiency are
  "good when down" -> green on a down arrow). fmtNumber/fmtInt/formatCurrency ported with
  en-US + precision-2 web defaults (WoWNumberFormat / WoWCurrency).
- States (every state renders — no hidden surfaces):
    loading  -> six-card skeleton grid (TSStatSkeleton; web DigestSkeleton)
    error    -> danger box + Retry affordance wired to model.refresh (QueryError-equivalent)
    empty    -> friendly "No activity this week" state (web parent !hasData branch)
    data     -> the six comparison cards
    stale    -> data + Stale chip + auto-refresh (onChange -> model.refresh)
    offline  -> cached data + Offline chip
- i18n: all 7 source keys (analytics.weeklyDigest.weekOverWeek/distance/drives/energy/cost/
  efficiency/co2) + native chrome (unit symbols, stale/offline/retry/error/empty, trend +
  loading a11y) resolve through the P1/S10 facade (WoWStrings, table "WeekOverWeekSummary",
  WeekOverWeekSummary.strings). No English string literals in native code.
- Accessibility: every card is one combined VoiceOver element (label, value, unit, trend
  phrase via WoWAccessibility.cardSummary); chips combine; icons accessibilityHidden;
  system fonts (Font.TS) scale with Dynamic Type; reduce-motion honored (TSFadeIn /
  TSStatSkeleton shimmer gated).
- Telemetry (P1/S11): WeekOverWeekModel.start emits view.opened with surface slug
  "WeekOverWeekSummary" exactly once (OSLogWeekOverWeekTelemetry -> screen_view; asserted).

