WHY [F]/[G] ARE BLOCKED (pre-existing + unrelated — not red-as-green)
------------------------------------------------------------
The iOS/macOS app targets (project.yml) source `TeslaSync/feature-views` with NO exclude
for `*.Tests.swift`, so the 25 PRE-EXISTING co-located test files in that directory
(AuditPanel.Tests.swift is alphabetically first) get compiled into the app target and fail
to resolve `XCTest` (XCTest is not linkable into an application). A second pre-existing
class of breakage — `public struct DashboardWidgetSize` redefined 15x across
Sources/DashboardWidgets/* + TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/* — would also block the link.
Both are documented, out-of-scope, pre-existing issues:

  apps/macos-pending-verifications.md, row "p4-apple/feature-views/P-0010-ToolCard":
    "Full-app iOS-Simulator + macOS xcodebuild build test … blocked by pre-existing,
     unrelated parallel-merge collisions — public struct DashboardWidgetSize (…) redefined
     8x …, co-located *.Tests.swift importing XCTest into the app target, and macOS
     development-signing. … The ToolCard surface itself is verified green (isolated SwiftPM
     build + 13/13 tests under Swift 6 strict concurrency; swiftlint/swiftformat/placeholder
     clean)." -> Status: macOS-pending.

This surface (also feature-views tier) is in exactly that documented posture: the surface
is verified GREEN by the isolated SwiftPM build + 37 tests + lint/format/placeholder; the
full-app `xcodebuild build test` is BLOCKED by pre-existing co-located-test + symbol-collision
breakage in OTHER files. Zero WeekOverWeekSummary errors appear in either full-app build.
The prompt's Allowed-files scope is WeekOverWeekSummary.* + this log, so the pre-existing
blockers (other surfaces' files + project.yml) are intentionally NOT modified.

